## Codebase Patterns

- `WebComponent` (from `@substrate-system/web-component`) uses
  `this.TAG` (an **instance** field) inside `emit()`/`on()`/`off()`,
  not the static `TAG`. Any subclass that only sets `static TAG = '...'`
  without also setting an instance field `TAG = '...'` will silently
  emit events namespaced as `:eventname` (empty prefix) instead of
  `tag-name:eventname`, and consumer listeners for the namespaced event
  will never fire. Always set both:
  ```ts
  export class Foo extends WebComponent {
      static TAG = 'foo'
      TAG = Foo.TAG
      ...
  }
  ```
  This was a latent bug in the original `image-input` scaffold (only
  `static TAG` was set) that had gone unnoticed because no test
  exercised a namespaced custom event before this session.
- Reflected attributes (`static reflectedStringAttributes` /
  `reflectedBooleanAttributes`) get auto-generated getters/setters by
  the base class's `define()`. Adding a name here is enough to get
  `this.foo` / `this.foo = x` working; you still write your own
  `handleChange_foo(oldValue, newValue)` for DOM side effects, which
  runs on `attributeChangedCallback`, not on `render()`. `render()`
  only runs once (from `connectedCallback`), so any post-mount state
  changes (alt text, preview image, overlay toggling) should mutate
  the existing DOM directly (via `this.qs(...)`) rather than
  re-invoking `render()`, or you will lose imperative state like the
  `<img>` `src` set from a file/object URL.
- CSS: `src/_vars.css` holds `:root` custom properties, imported by
  `src/index.css` via `@import './_vars.css'`. The `build-css` /
  `build-css:min` npm scripts now pass `--bundle` to `lightningcss` so
  the import is inlined into `dist/index.css` (bundler CLI does not
  resolve `@import` by default, only with `--bundle`). Keep this flag
  if more CSS partials are added later (e.g. for `crop.ts`).
- Preview images use `URL.createObjectURL(file)` (not `FileReader`
  data URLs) so the same object-URL lifecycle/revocation pattern can
  be reused by `image-crop` later. Always revoke the previous object
  URL before creating a new one and on remove, to avoid leaking blobs.
- Test pattern for simulating a file input: build a `DataTransfer`,
  `dataTransfer.items.add(file)`, assign `input.files =
  dataTransfer.files`, then `input.dispatchEvent(new Event('change',
  { bubbles: true }))`. See `test/index.ts` `selectFile()` helper.
- No "dev-browser" skill is registered in this harness. Use the
  Playwright MCP tools directly against `npm run start` (vite dev
  server) for the "verify in browser" acceptance criteria, and kill
  the dev server + delete the `.playwright-mcp/` scratch directory
  afterwards (it is not gitignored and holds screenshots/snapshots
  that shouldn't be committed).
- `test/index.html` (the tape-run harness) does NOT load
  `src/index.css` -- only `test-bundle.js`. Any component whose
  correctness depends on real layout (not just class-presence
  assertions) cannot rely on external stylesheet rules like
  `display:block` or `width:100%` being applied during tests.
  Compute pixel dimensions in JS from `this.clientWidth` etc. and
  set them as inline styles rather than depending on the stylesheet,
  and force a deterministic box size in tests via an inline
  `style="display:block;width:...px"` on the host element.

